  "comparability_note": {
    "verdict": "WITHIN-COUMN IS NOT COMPARABLE TO KRASNOV 2026. The two use different cohorts.",
    "ours": "within_metal_cv is 5-fold CV on the LOMO dedup cohort (Ru n_unique=1255 pos_rate 0.2574; Ir n_unique=534 pos_rate 0.4532).",
    "krasnov": "Their 0.81 / 0.73 come from a cancer-only cohort of 15,799 rows / 4,793 complexes / 591 cell lines (see metalcytotox_ru_auc.json::paper_protocol_measurement).",
    "our_number_on_their_cohort": "0.7717 +/- 0.0380 under their DOI-split 10-fold CV, which is 0.0383 BELOW their LightGBM 0.810 +/- 0.024, with 3/10 folds at or above. That is the only like-for-like comparison on disk.",
    "tie_sensitivity": "Both sides use the identical collapse predicate (sum*2 >= n, ties -> ACTIVE), so the tie rule does not confound the cross-metal comparison. It DOES move the within column: conservative rule gives Ru 0.7880-0.8082 (at or below Krasnov 0.81) while Ir is unchanged and stays above 0.73 under both rules and all 5 seeds.",
    "withdrawn": "The CLAIM 'within-metal matches or beats the published result' is WITHDRAWN for Ru. It is defensible for Ir only.",
    "supersedes_a_bad_citation": "todo.json::withdrawn_claims_2026_10_10 justified this withdrawal by citing 'DOI-grouped 0.6350 / 0.6065'. Those two numbers DO NOT EXIST anywhere on disk; the only 0.6351 in the repo is an Os per-seed value in metal_lomo_auc.json, a different experiment. The withdrawal conclusion is correct; that citation was not traceable."
  }
